    "principles": [
      {
        "id": "principle-21aeca67",
        "title": "Develop around a few must haves first and plan around them",
        "description": "We wanted to do the Kalalau trail and camp at the beach.  We also wanted to see Waimea canyon.  Both of those required permits from the state with ample lead time.  These activities were on opposite sides of the island by road, so this lead to a natural path between the two."
      },
      {
        "id": "principle-ca671859",
        "title": "Alternate between roughing it in the tent and luxury accomodations",
        "description": "So much easier to do that second camping trip after a few days in a comfortable bed with a full stomach."
      },
      {
        "id": "principle-5606fe74",
        "title": "Be honest with yourself about your level of effort and number of activities",
        "description": "We knew we could handle the hikes and the camping.  I still left room in the schedule for spontaneous decisions, like our visit to Kauaian Coffee and Ho'opi'i Falls"
      }
